{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/unicode-org/icu4x/pulls/8144","id":3940983139,"node_id":"PR_kwDODoHqRc7q5qFj","html_url":"https://github.com/unicode-org/icu4x/pull/8144","diff_url":"https://github.com/unicode-org/icu4x/pull/8144.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/unicode-org/icu4x/pull/8144.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/unicode-org/icu4x/issues/8144","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/unicode-org/icu4x/pulls/8144/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/unicode-org/icu4x/pulls/8144/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/unicode-org/icu4x/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/unicode-org/icu4x/issues/8144/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/unicode-org/icu4x/statuses/33a4116e387f7027348a0542a18bf3108fd662ab","number":8144,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Reduce allocations for complex segmenter runs","user":{"login":"Xuanwo","id":5351546,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzNTE1NDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5351546?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xuanwo","html_url":"https://github.com/Xuanwo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xuanwo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xuanwo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xuanwo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xuanwo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xuanwo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xuanwo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xuanwo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xuanwo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xuanwo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\r\n\r\nThe V1 word and line segmenters previously copied every complex-script run into a temporary `String` or `Vec<u16>` before dictionary or LSTM segmentation. This keeps one original `Y::IterAttr` and slices it by the run's absolute offsets instead.\r\n\r\nThis is encoding-generic rather than a `str` specialization:\r\n\r\n- `Utf8` slices `CharIndices::as_str()` with byte offsets.\r\n- `PotentiallyIllFormedUtf8` slices `Utf8CharIndices::as_slice()` with byte offsets.\r\n- `Utf16` slices `Utf16Indices::as_slice()` with code unit offsets.\r\n\r\nPotentially ill-formed UTF-8 is passed through the byte-based complex segmenter, where `Utf8CharIndices` preserves replacement-character semantics. UTF-16 continues to preserve unpaired surrogates in the outer rule iterator. The implementation covers published word segmentation and both V1 and V3 line segmentation; the V2/neo path already slices `Y::IterAttr` directly.\r\n\r\nNo public API changes are introduced.\r\n\r\n## Performance\r\n\r\nBaseline: `origin/main` at `72bbff74dc`. Current: `33a4116e38`.\r\n\r\nThe representative workloads and dictionary constructors come from the merged segmenter benchmarks: `Ja` for word segmentation and `Th` for line segmentation. The baseline includes the result-cache consumption optimization from #8143. A matching local probe covers raw `segment_utf8`, which is not currently included in the Criterion harness, and reports allocations per complete segmentation call. Probe times are medians of three alternating baseline/current release runs with 1,000 warm-up calls and 250,000 measured calls.\r\n\r\n| Workload | Allocations before | Allocations after | Bytes before | Bytes after | Time before | Time after | Time delta |\r\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\r\n| word `segment_str` / Ja | 8 | 3 | 472 | 224 | 1.520 us | 1.359 us | -10.6% |\r\n| word `segment_utf8` / Ja | 8 | 3 | 472 | 224 | 1.631 us | 1.581 us | -3.1% |\r\n| word `segment_utf16` / Ja | 9 | 3 | 474 | 224 | 1.431 us | 1.265 us | -11.6% |\r\n| line `segment_str` / Th | 30 | 6 | 912 | 192 | 2.711 us | 2.010 us | -25.9% |\r\n| line `segment_utf8` / Th | 30 | 6 | 912 | 192 | 2.934 us | 2.446 us | -16.6% |\r\n| line `segment_utf16` / Th | 30 | 6 | 540 | 192 | 2.295 us | 1.781 us | -22.4% |\r\n\r\nThe merged Criterion harness independently reports:\r\n\r\n| Criterion case | Before | After | Delta |\r\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\r\n| Word Break/UTF8/Ja/dictionary | 1.468 us | 1.331 us | -9.3% |\r\n| Word Break/UTF16/Ja/dictionary | 1.423 us | 1.296 us | -8.9% |\r\n| Line Break/UTF8/Th/dictionary | 2.621 us | 1.981 us | -24.4% |\r\n| Line Break/UTF16/Th/dictionary | 2.312 us | 1.852 us | -19.9% |\r\n\r\nThe cache stress benchmarks added by #8143 confirm that the two optimizations compose:\r\n\r\n| Criterion case, 16K chars | Before | After | Delta |\r\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\r\n| Full word segmentation, continuous Han | 857.4 us | 483.2 us | -43.6% |\r\n| Full line segmentation, continuous Thai | 342.9 us | 335.6 us | -2.1% |\r\n| First 10 word boundaries, continuous Han | 817.2 us | 457.8 us | -44.0% |\r\n| First 10 line boundaries, continuous Thai | 321.6 us | 309.8 us | -3.7% |\r\n\r\n## Changelog\r\n\r\n`icu_segmenter`: Performance improvements for complex word and line segmenters.\r\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-06-26T08:31:46Z","updated_at":"2026-08-31T11:53:00Z","closed_at":"2026-08-31T11:52:35Z","merged_at":"2026-08-31T11:52:35Z","merge_commit_sha":"a9cbb9cda7cc0b1e832ace6a0f633fc6a3f3726d","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"aethanyc","id":102858,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMjg1OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/102858?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aethanyc","html_url":"https://github.com/aethanyc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aethanyc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aethanyc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aethanyc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aethanyc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aethanyc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aethanyc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aethanyc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aethanyc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aethanyc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},{"login":"makotokato","id":965338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2NTMzOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/965338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/makotokato","html_url":"https://github.com/makotokato","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/makotokato/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/makotokato/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/makotokato/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/makotokato/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/makotokato/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/makotokato/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/makotokato/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/makotokato/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/makotokato/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},{"login":"sffc","id":1145762,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNDU3NjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1145762?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sffc","html_url":"https://github.com/sffc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sffc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sffc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sffc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sffc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sffc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sffc/orgs","repos_url